@format 1
@id media-preview.in-global-interface
@title In Global interface
@section Media preview
@area In Global interface
@entry startup-restore, relay-source
@summary Show global operations that directly request a source in the active/relay preview viewer without adding it to a Files docket.
@related media-preview.common.viewer-gate, media-preview.common.media-publication
@tag media
@tag preview
@tag global

@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace

[startup-restore] Automatic startup preview restore <input>
~ This starts with automatic startup preview restore.
[Technical explanation]
- Require automatic restore, a nonblank saved path, and an existing file, then queue a Loaded-priority callback that calls PViewerSourceOpen on the viewer active when the callback executes @ window.PWindowMediaRestore(...)
> startup-result

[relay-source] Relay source arrival <input>
~ This starts with transfer source arrival.
[Technical explanation]
- Create and select the relay tab, then apply its relay payload to the selected workspace @ window.PWindowRelayAccept(...)
  @ workspace.PWorkspaceRelayApply(...)
> relay-result

[startup-result] Startup restore outcome <decision>
~ The program checks whether a saved startup media path was restored.
[Technical explanation]
- Continue only when the preconditions caused the viewer-open callback to be queued and an active viewer exists when it executes @ window.PWindowMediaRestore(...)
? "PViewerSourceOpen called" > map:media-preview.common.viewer-gate
? "No restorable/active viewer source" > startup-stop

[relay-result] Relay preview outcome <decision>
~ The program checks whether the transferred media should be shown in the preview.
[Technical explanation]
- PWorkspaceRelayApply requires a viewer and nonblank relay source; before calling PViewerSourceOpen it installs a one-shot PViewerMediaChange handler for later section restoration @ workspace.PWorkspaceRelayApply(...)
? "Viewer call issued" > map:media-preview.common.viewer-gate
? "No viewer or blank relay source" > relay-stop

[startup-stop] Startup preview restore skipped <output>
~ This path ends with startup preview restore skipped.
[Technical explanation]
= No shared viewer request is made.

[relay-stop] Relay has no preview request <output>
~ This path ends with transfer has no preview request.
[Technical explanation]
= No temporary relay media handler is installed and PViewerSourceOpen is not called.
! Once the one-shot relay handler has been installed, a later PViewerSourceOpen rejection that raises no media event can leave that handler attached until a later viewer-media event occurs.
